    sections: [
        (name: "The Net", cards: [
            (title: "Welcome to the Net", picture: Some("deck"), text: [
                "Congratulations on your new Sense/Net Personal Deck!",
                "",
                "Your deck connects you to the Net: the vast, humming",
                "web of computers that runs the modern world.",
                "",
                "This stack will show you around. Use the arrows to",
                "turn the page, or Home to pick a section.",
            ]),
            (title: "Millions every day", picture: Some("net"), text: [
                "Every day, millions of people do business on the Net.",
                "Most reach it through their company's dial-up: a",
                "phone number, a modem, and a password from IT.",
                "",
                "Banks, shippers, labs and laundries all keep their",
                "machines on the line, day and night.",
            ]),
            (title: "Who's out there", picture: Some("corp"), text: [
                "CORPS run their own networks, and the biggest of them,",
                "the megacorps, run the backbones everyone else uses.",
                "",
                "SYSOPS run bulletin boards: little systems you can",
                "call for files, news and conversation.",
                "",
                "THE TELCO owns the lines, and keeps a record of every",
                "call.",
            ]),
            (title: "Hackers", picture: Some("ice"), text: [
                "You may hear a new word on the Net: HACKERS.",
                "",
                "Pranksters and criminals, they call themselves",
                "hackers. They break into company systems for fun,",
                "for money, or to see if they can.",
                "",
                "They form groups with strange names, and run illicit",
                "bulletin boards on the Net to share what they know:",
                "numbers, programs, ways in.",
                "",
                "Sense/Net does not support these activities.",
            ]),
        ]),
        (name: "Dialing in", cards: [
            (title: "The phonebook", picture: Some("phone"), text: [
                "Every network sits behind a phone number. The numbers",
                "you know live in CarrierTerm's phonebook.",
                "",
                "Dial one and your deck connects. Your deck came with",
                "a few numbers to start.",
                "",
                "Some numbers are bulletin boards you can call from",
                "home. Each call costs {call_cost}¢ on your phone bill.",
            ]),
            (title: "New numbers", picture: Some("phone"), text: [
                "You'll come across new numbers as you go: in data,",
                "on bulletin boards, from the people you meet.",
                "",
                "Write them down. A number is the only way back.",
            ]),
        ]),
        (name: "A run", cards: [
            (title: "Layers", picture: Some("net"), text: [
                "A network is built in layers. You come in at the",
                "gateway and work your way down, node by node, to the",
                "exit on the far side.",
                "",
                "Most nodes are quiet: stores of data, a board, a",
                "contact who'd like a word. Some are guarded.",
                "",
                "The gateway closes behind you. The only way out is on.",
            ]),
            (title: "Trace", picture: Some("trace"), text: [
                "Networks keep an eye on who's connected. Wander where",
                "you aren't expected and they start tracing your line.",
                "",
                "At {trace_max}% they've found you, and your deck drops off",
                "the Net. Sense/Net calls this a service interruption.",
            ]),
        ]),
        (name: "ICE", cards: [
            (title: "Intrusion countermeasures", picture: Some("ice"), text: [
                "Companies protect their systems with ICE: security",
                "programs that keep strangers out. There are three",
                "kinds:",
                "",
                "  BARRIERS hold the line.",
                "  CODE GATES ask for a password.",
                "  SENTRIES watch for trouble.",
                "",
                "If ICE stops you, you're somewhere you shouldn't be.",
            ]),
            (title: "Black ICE", picture: Some("ice"), text: [
                "The biggest companies run black ICE. It is stronger,",
                "and it does not stop at your deck.",
                "",
                "Sense/Net recommends you turn back.",
            ]),
        ]),
        (name: "Boards & work", cards: [
            (title: "Bulletin boards", picture: Some("bbs"), text: [
                "Some nodes are BBSes. Connect and you can read the",
                "bulletins, download files, see who's online, and",
                "take jobs. Once you've connected, its number is yours.",
                "",
                "Some are friendly little hangouts. Some would rather",
                "you weren't there at all.",
            ]),
            (title: "Contracts", picture: Some("contract"), text: [
                "Many boards carry a jobs board, where clients post",
                "work and pay on completion.",
                "",
                "Sense/Net is not responsible for third-party clients",
                "who fail to honour agreements.",
            ]),
        ]),
        (name: "Your deck", cards: [
            (title: "Making it yours", picture: Some("deck"), text: [
                "Your deck starts with {cpu} CPU, {ram} GB of RAM, {hdd} disk",
                "slots and {integrity} integrity. RIG sells upgrades.",
                "Your stash keeps {stash} programs you bring home safe.",
                "",
                "Better decks exist. Ask at RIG.",
            ]),
            (title: "That's the tour", picture: Some("deck"), text: [
                "That's everything you need to get started.",
                "",
                "Open CarrierTerm, pick a number, and dial.",
                "",
                "This stack lives on your desktop if you need it again.",
                "",
                "Have a safe and productive session!",
                "                                       -- Sense/Net",
            ]),
        ]),
    ],
)
